==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-come across.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|come<,,came,come> across}}

# {{&lit|en|come|across}}
#: ''He '''came across''' the street towards me.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} To [[change]] [[sides]]; to cross over to work for the opposition.
#: {{ux|en|You argued well in court but your firm doesn't pay its lawyers well, so why don't you '''come across''' to ours?}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To give an [[appearance]] or [[impression]]; to project a certain [[image]].
#: {{ux|en|A business suit and briefcase help her to '''come across''' as the competent professional she is.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[find]], usually by [[accident]].
#: {{ux|en|In the meadow he '''came across''' a rare flower.}}
# To produce what was desired; [[come up with the goods]].
#* '''1929''', Reginald Charles Barker, ''The Hair-trigger Brand'' (page 160)
#*: "I'll die before I let my grandad pay you that much money!" blazed the girl.<br>"That ain't unlikely either," retorted Shanan, "if ol' Bart Hendricks don't '''come across''' with the ransom."

